{"type":"message","id":"35bbe591","parentId":"fcc5056a","timestamp":"2026-02-16T15:51:22.325Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The PowerShell commands have syntax issues with dot notation in script blocks. Let me simplify: I'll just list all json files in the .openclaw directory manually using a different syntax.\n\nThe first command worked: Get-ChildItem C:\\Users\\mangs\\.openclaw\\credentials\\whatsapp\\default -Force | Select-Object Name, Length, LastWriteTime\nIt showed only creds.json, size 1731, last write 2/16/2026 9:14:38 PM. That's the credentials file we already read.\n\nThe second command failed due to syntax: .Name instead of $_.Name. But we can fix that.\n\nHowever, I think I have enough to provide a diagnosis. The WhatsApp credentials exist but show registered: false. That's the core problem.\n\nLet me check if there are any other json files that might contain WhatsApp state. I'll try a corrected PowerShell command.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me search for any other WhatsApp-related configuration with a corrected command:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_df4b46944ff74b8aab2c1681","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -Command \"Get-ChildItem C:\\Users\\mangs\\.openclaw -Filter *.json | Select-Object FullName, LastWriteTime | Format-Table -AutoSize\"","pty":true}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":51171,"output":485,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51656,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771257076917}}
