{"type":"message","id":"a9850984","parentId":"de913bdc","timestamp":"2026-02-16T15:51:32.369Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"These are the JSON files in the root .openclaw directory. TheWhatsApp-specific creds are in the credentials subdirectory.\n\nNow, what about the logs? Maybe there are log files with other extensions or in subdirectories. Let me check the logs directory again.\n\nAlso, I need to check if the gateway is currently running. The openclaw.json shows gateway.port=18789, mode local. I could try to see if anything is listening on that port to confirm if the gateway is running.\n\nBut the main issue is clear: registered: false in the WhatsApp credentials. This prevents messages from being sent or received.\n\nNow, to provide a complete diagnosis, I should try to understand why it's false. There might be an error when trying to register. The OpenClaw project might have documentation on how to register WhatsApp. Since I can't search the web, I'll rely on what's present.\n\nThe credentials file includes:\n- noiseKey (private/public)\n- pairingEphemeralKeyPair\n- signedIdentityKey\n- signedPreKey with signature and keyId=1\n- registrationId: 159\n- advSecretKey\n- processedHistoryMessages: []\n- nextPreKeyId: 1\n- firstUnuploadedPreKeyId: 1\n- accountSyncCounter: 0\n- accountSettings\n- registered: false\n- account with details and signatures\n- me (user JID)\n- lid (linked device ID)\n- platform: android\n- signalIdentities\n\nThis looks like a full set of Signal keys for WhatsApp. The registration process likely requires sending these keys to WhatsApp's server and receiving a confirmation. Maybe the account creation was started but not completed. The presence of account details suggests something was done.\n\nGiven the `registered: false`, the WhatsApp plugin probably cannot send messages because it's not authenticated with the WhatsApp servers.\n\nNow, what are the recommended fixes? Likely:\n1. Re-register the WhatsApp account by going through the pairing process again (e.g., scan QR code or enter verification code).\n2. Ensure that the OpenClaw gateway is running and can reach WhatsApp's servers.\n3. Check that the credentials file is not corrupted.\n\nSince I'm a subagent, I should also attempt to test if messages can be sent/received, but that's not possible with registered:false. I could attempt to trigger a registration check or see if there's a command to register.\n\nMaybe I can check the config-audit.jsonl for entries related to WhatsApp plugin or credentials. Let me read that file more thoroughly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me read the full config-audit log to see if there were any WhatsApp-related changes or errors:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5fafd638eb3e4ae4866ad355","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"C:/Users/mangs/.openclaw/logs/config-audit.jsonl","limit":100}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":51666,"output":1231,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":52897,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771257083784}}
