{"type":"message","id":"e381b251","parentId":"59a666d0","timestamp":"2026-02-16T15:56:34.232Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The PowerShell command had a syntax issue. Let me fix it and try again. But I can see from the creds.json that `\"registered\":false` - this means the WhatsApp account is NOT registered. That's a key finding! The credentials exist but the account is not registered with WhatsApp. That explains why it's not working.\n\nAlso, I see that the credentials have a WhatsApp user ID (918798546282:45@s.whatsapp.net) and it's in a pairing state with Signal protocol keys.\n\nLet me fix the PowerShell command to get more details.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me fix the PowerShell command:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9b7f92772cd04e729169c58b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -Command \"$creds = Get-Content C:\\Users\\mangs\\.openclaw\\credentials\\whatsapp\\default\\creds.json | ConvertFrom-Json; Write-Host 'Registered:' $creds.registered; Write-Host 'User ID:' $creds.me.id; Write-Host 'Platform:' $creds.platform; Write-Host 'Account Synced:' $creds.accountSyncCounter\"","pty":true}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6a79a8d2e48447ca823cc94a","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"C:/Users/mangs/.openclaw/openclaw.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":86335,"output":413,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86748,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771257386597}}
