true,\n        \"maxChars\": 50000,\n        \"timeoutSeconds\": 45,\n        \"maxRedirects\": 5\n      }\n    },\n    \"media\": {\n      \"image\": {\n        \"enabled\": true,\n        \"maxBytes\": 5242880,\n        \"maxChars\": 2000,\n        \"timeoutSeconds\": 60\n      }\n    },\n    \"message\": {\n      \"allowCrossContextSend\": true,\n      \"crossContext\": {\n        \"allowWithinProvider\": true,\n        \"allowAcrossProviders\": false\n      }\n    },\n    \"exec\": {\n      \"host\": \"gateway\",\n      \"security\": \"full\",\n      \"ask\": \"off\",\n      \"backgroundMs\": 10000,\n      \"timeoutSec\": 300,\n      \"applyPatch\": {\n        \"enabled\": true,\n        \"workspaceOnly\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"fs\": {\n      \"workspaceOnly\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"commands\": {\n    \"native\": \"auto\",\n    \"nativeSkills\": \"auto\",\n    \"restart\": true\n  },\n  \"gateway\": {\n    \"port\": 18789,\n    \"mode\": \"local\",\n    \"controlUi\": {\n      \"dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth\": true\n    },\n    \"auth\": {\n      \"mode\": \"token\",\n      \"token\": \"openclaw-token\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"plugins\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"entries\": {\n      \"whatsapp\": {\n        \"enabled\": true\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771257395741}}
{"type":"message","id":"83f1f28b","parentId":"8999005d","timestamp":"2026-02-16T15:56:50.415Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I can see the config shows the WhatsApp plugin is enabled. But there's no specific plugin configuration beyond that. The creds.json shows registered: false, which is the core issue.\n\nLet me check the execution approvals and try to understand the current state better. Also, let me write a comprehensive diagnostic summary for the user with the findings and recommendations.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Based on my diagnostic investigation, I can now provide a comprehensive report on the WhatsApp channel issue. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## WhatsApp Channel Diagnostic Report\n\n### 🔍 **Findings**\n\n**1. WhatsApp Plugin Configuration**\n- ✅ Plugin is **enabled** in `openclaw.json`: `\"plugins\": {\"entries\": {\"whatsapp\": {\"enabled\": true}}}`\n- ✅ Credentials file exists: `C:\\Users\\mangs\\.openclaw\\credentials\\whatsapp\\default\\creds.json`\n- ⚠️ **CRITICAL**: WhatsApp account is **NOT registered** (`\"registered\": false`)\n- The credential file contains Signal protocol keys and user info, indicating pairing was initiated but not completed\n\n**2. Gateway Logs Analysis**\n- Config audit log shows recent restarts and config changes\n- No explicit WhatsApp errors found in the limited logs (only `config-audit.jsonl` exists)\n- The \"WhatsApp QR received\" message you mentioned at 21:24:28 indicates the plugin successfully generated a QR code for pairing\n\n**3. WhatsApp Account Pairing Status**\n- **Status**: Pending/Incomplete\n- User ID: `918798546282:45@s.whatsapp.net`\n- Platform: Android\n- Account sync counter: 0 (no sync activity)\n- **The QR code was generated but likely not scanned or the pairing didn't complete**\n\n**4. Recent Configuration Changes**\n- Multiple config writes on Feb 16 between 06:11-15:50\n- Final config update at 15:50:41 from workspace directory\n- No WhatsApp-specific config changes detected (only general openclaw.json changes)\n\n**5. Message Sending Capability**\n- **Cannot send/receive messages** because account is not registered\n- The WhatsApp connection is in a pre-paired state waiting for QR code scan completion\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ **Recommended Fixes**\n\n**Immediate Action Required:**\n\n1. **Complete WhatsApp Pairing**\n   - Access the OpenClaw web UI (usually http://localhost:18789)\n   - Navigate to the WhatsApp plugin section\n   - **Scan the displayed QR code with your WhatsApp mobile app**\n   - Ensure you scan it promptly (QR codes have expiration)\n   - Wait for the \"paired\" confirmation\n\n2. **Verify Pairing Success**\n   - After scanning, check that `creds.json` updates with `\"registered\": true`\n   - Look for success logs indicating connection establishment\n   - Try sending a test message\n\n3. **If QR Code Expired or Issues Persist**\n   - Restart the gateway to regenerate QR: `openclaw gateway restart`\n   - Clear the WhatsApp credentials to start fresh:\n     ```powershell\n     Remove-Item C:\\Users\\mangs\\.openclaw\\credentials\\whatsapp\\default -Recurse -Force\n     ```\n   - Then restart gateway and re-pair\n\n---\n\n### 💾 **Memory Search Embedding Provider Recommendation**\n\nFor memory search functionality, you need an embedding provider with an API key. Here are the options:\n\n**Recommendation: OpenAI Embeddings**\n- **Why**: Most reliable, good quality, well-documented\n- **Cost**: ~$0.0001 per 1K tokens (very affordable)\n- **Setup**: Add to `openclaw.json`:\n  ```json\n  \"memory\": {\n    \"embedding\": {\n      \"provider\": \"openai\",\n      \"apiKey\": \"sk-...\"\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n\n**Alternative: Google AI (if you have Google Cloud)**\n- Good quality, competitive pricing\n- Requires Google Cloud account and API key\n\n**Note**: OpenRouter only provides LLM APIs, **not embeddings**. You need a separate embedding provider.\n\n---\n\n### 📋 **Next Steps**\n\n1. **First**: Complete WhatsApp QR scanning via web UI\n2. **Test**: Send a test message after pairing\n3. **Configure**: Choose and add an embedding provider for memory search\n4. **Monitor**: Check `C:\\Users\\mangs\\.openclaw\\logs\\` for any plugin-specific logs if issues persist\n\nWould you like me to help you access the web UI to find the QR code, or assist with configuring the embedding provider once you decide which one to use?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":87676,"output":1072,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88748,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1771257395744}}
